# Shell scripts must stay LF — bash chokes on CRLF
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python source should stay LF across platforms so that Windows checkouts
# don't get warned at every git operation ("LF will be replaced by CRLF")
# and so that tooling (ruff, mypy, pytest) sees consistent line endings.
*.py text eol=lf

# Text-only config and docs — same reasoning as Python.
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf

# The automation register is a catalogue regenerated from the repository, so
# every branch rewrites its tallies and appends its own rows in the same place.
# Measured 2026-09-18: of ten open branches that could not merge, SEVEN collided
# here and one collided on nothing else at all.
#
# The driver TAKES ONE SIDE WHOLE and never unions. Every side of a conflict
# here is a stale rendering and the row SET is recoverable by regeneration, so
# taking one loses nothing a regeneration cannot restore. What it does NOT
# claim is that both sides render the same fact: they render different branch
# histories. A deadlock-breaker, not a cure. The driver's own docstring carries
# the measurement, the confound that broke the first argument, and the limit.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-09-23. Found by Aria reading arc one; confirmed by Aether
# reading the driver rather than taking her word. This paragraph described a
# design that no longer exists -- it said the driver keeps BOTH sides' rows and
# REFUSES on partial overlap. That was the first version. The driver records
# that union_resolve is deliberately not imported any more, and its output line
# reads "took one side whole".
#
# A sign pointing at a demolished room, and the FIRST thing a reader of the
# merge rule meets. The new behaviour was added and the old description never
# taken out -- the same shape as three other findings the same night.
#
# The driver itself is registered per-clone by setup/setup-hooks.sh. This line
# alone does nothing: a clone that has not run setup finds no driver by this
# name and falls back to ordinary merging, which fails toward the conflict
# rather than toward a silent resolution.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT APPLIED to CLAUDE.md or the architecture map, which collide
# the same way and which the underlying resolver was originally written for.
# Those are part hand-authored, and union-merging a hand-written rule keeps both
# halves of two people editing it.
docs/AUTOMATION_REGISTER.md merge=catalogue

# graphify outputs are machine-generated maps of the OS. Kept in-repo (they
# ARE the map — see graphify-out/README.md). Marked linguist-generated so
# GitHub collapses them in PR diffs, keeping the reviewable diff legible
# while the map still ships. Aletheia audit 2026-07-13; Andrew authorized.
graphify-out*/graph.json linguist-generated=true
graphify-out*/graph.html linguist-generated=true
graphify-out*/GRAPH_REPORT.md linguist-generated=true
graphify-out*/cache/** linguist-generated=true
